+ '</code></pre></div></div>'
+ '<p class="l-text"><strong>What the label dictionaries do:</strong> 1) The 9-label inventory (<code>O</code> plus B/I variants of <code>PER</code>, <code>ORG</code>, <code>LOC</code>, <code>MISC</code>) covers everything CoNLL-2003 annotates. 2) <code>label2id</code> maps each string tag to the integer index the model\'s classification head will output. 3) <code>id2label = {v: k for k, v in label2id.items()}</code> inverts the mapping so you can decode model predictions back to readable BIO tags. 4) Both dicts are passed to <code>AutoModelForTokenClassification.from_pretrained(..., id2label=..., label2id=...)</code> so the model carries the label names with it — essential for the <code>pipeline()</code> API to return human-readable entities at inference.</p>'
